WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Mowgli followed the woman into her hut.

2
00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:08.421
He felt nervous, but the woman seemed kind.

3
00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:10.871
Inside the hut was a bed.

4
00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:16.548
He also saw a large chest for storing grain and copper cooking pots.

5
00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:21.406
Hanging on the wall were images of gods and a tall glass.

6
00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:26.733
When Mowgli stepped in front of the glass, he gasped.

7
00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:31.420
"Another boy lives here!" he thought in surprise.

8
00:00:31.421 --> 00:00:33.587
He lifted an arm.

9
00:00:33.588 --> 00:00:36.152
So did the boy in the glass.

10
00:00:36.153 --> 00:00:38.689
Mowgli wiggled his fingers.

11
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:43.794
Again the boy did just what Mowgli was doing.

12
00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:46.894
The woman laughed.

13
00:00:46.895 --> 00:00:50.112
She pointed from Mowgli to the mirror.

14
00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:58.420
"Oh!" Finally Mowgli understood. "That's me in the glass!"

15
00:00:58.421 --> 00:01:01.948
The woman gave him some milk and bread.

16
00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:05.399
Then she lay her hand on his head.

17
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.692
"Nathoo? Do you remember the shoes I gave you?"

18
00:01:10.693 --> 00:01:14.751
Mowgli shook his head, unable to understand.

19
00:01:14.752 --> 00:01:20.711
The woman touched his foot. It felt as hard as an animal horn.

20
00:01:20.712 --> 00:01:23.671
"No," she said sadly.

21
00:01:23.672 --> 00:01:27.101
"These feet have never worn shoes.

22
00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:33.270
But you look like my Nathoo, and you shall be my son."

23
00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:37.109
Mowgli had never been under a roof before.

24
00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:43.434
He climbed on a stool to touch the straw over his head.

25
00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:46.631
The hut had a door and a window.

26
00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:50.734
But he could also rip the roof's straw if he felt trapped.

27
00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:53.502
That thought eased his mind.

28
00:01:53.503 --> 00:01:56.385
But something else was bothering him.

29
00:01:56.386 --> 00:02:00.567
"I must learn the humans' language," he realized.

30
00:02:00.568 --> 00:02:06.149
"I cannot live with people if I don’t understand their words."

31
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:11.804
So as soon as Messua pronounced a word, Mowgli repeated it.

32
00:02:11.805 --> 00:02:17.872
Before dark he had learned the names of many things in the hut.

33
00:02:17.873 --> 00:02:25.630
At bedtime Messua and her husband shut the door to the hut.

34
00:02:25.631 --> 00:02:31.632
Mowgli felt trapped.

35
00:02:31.633 --> 00:02:36.345
He quickly slipped through a window.

36
00:02:36.346 --> 00:02:39.946
"I must fetch him!" Messua said.

37
00:02:39.947 --> 00:02:44.962
Her husband stopped her. "Leave him alone," he said.

38
00:02:44.963 --> 00:02:47.709
"The boy has never slept on a bed before.

39
00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:53.908
If he is indeed our son, he won't run away."

40
00:02:53.909 --> 00:03:01.522
Mowgli stretched out in some long grass at the edge of the field.

41
00:03:01.523 --> 00:03:09.550
Before he could close his eyes, a soft gray nose poked him.

42
00:03:09.551 --> 00:03:13.854
"Gray Brother!" Mowgli cried in delight.

43
00:03:13.855 --> 00:03:16.492
The wolf sniffed Mowgli.

44
00:03:16.493 --> 00:03:18.839
"Yuck!" he said.

45
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.494
"This is a terrible reward for following you.

46
00:03:22.495 --> 00:03:27.637
You smell like wood smoke and cattle—human smells!"

47
00:03:27.638 --> 00:03:34.085
Mowgli laughed. "Is everything okay?"

48
00:03:34.086 --> 00:03:38.172
"Not exactly," Gray Brother replied.

49
00:03:38.173 --> 00:03:41.179
"I have news about Shere Khan.

50
00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.882
He's gone off to hunt for a while.

51
00:03:43.883 --> 00:03:47.081
But the red flower burned him badly.

52
00:03:47.082 --> 00:03:51.037
He promises to hunt you down when he returns.

53
00:03:51.038 --> 00:03:54.626
He wants to lay your bones in the river!"

54
00:03:54.627 --> 00:03:58.405
"He doesn't scare me," Mowgli said.

55
00:03:58.406 --> 00:04:05.550
"I'm going to hunt him down one day! Even Mother Wolf says that's true."

56
00:04:05.551 --> 00:04:08.234
Gray Brother looked worried.

57
00:04:08.235 --> 00:04:13.283
"Shere Khan is very dangerous, Mowgli. Be careful."

58
00:04:13.284 --> 00:04:18.799
"I'll be careful." Mowgli yawned.

59
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:24.226
"I'm so tired tonight. I learned many new things today.

60
00:04:24.227 --> 00:04:28.782
Please bring me more news soon."

61
00:04:28.783 --> 00:04:31.895
His eyes closed for a moment.

62
00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:37.747
"You won't forget that you're a wolf, will you?" Gray Brother asked anxiously.

63
00:04:37.748 --> 00:04:40.501
"Never," Mowgli promised.

64
00:04:40.502 --> 00:04:45.306
"I will always remember that I love you and our cave.

65
00:04:45.307 --> 00:04:48.635
But you must remember something, Gray Brother.

66
00:04:48.636 --> 00:04:52.157
The wolf pack cast me out."

67
00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:56.926
"The man pack could cast you out too," Gray Brother said.

68
00:04:56.927 --> 00:05:00.077
"People are only people, Mowgli.

69
00:05:00.078 --> 00:05:05.996
Their talk is like the talk of frogs in a pond. It doesn't mean much."

70
00:05:05.997 --> 00:05:10.164
Mowgli shrugged. His eyes closed again.

71
00:05:10.165 --> 00:05:14.375
"I will let you sleep," Gray Brother said finally.

72
00:05:14.376 --> 00:05:16.462
"I'll come again in a few weeks.

73
00:05:16.463 --> 00:05:18.703
Look for me in the bamboo.

74
00:05:18.704 --> 00:05:23.166
It's at the edge of the people's fields."

75
00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:29.248
"Okay," Mowgli whispered. "Good night."

